{
  "area": "jamaica",
  "method": "Jamaica's north and west coast resort areas: Negril, Montego Bay (with Lucea), Ocho Rios and Runaway Bay; Kingston and Port Royal were searched but no operator list was readable. No official list was found: the Montego Bay Marine Park Trust and Negril Marine Park publish no mooring or dive-site list, and NEPA has none online (the Trust site did not resolve), so the Jamaica Tourist Board's caves page (visitjamaica.com, counted as one list) is the only government-tied list and names just two sites. Operator lists read: ScubaCaribe (its Negril, Montego Bay and Ocho Rios dive-site map PDFs and web pages, which are for RIU guests), Negril Adventure Divers (Wayback snapshot), Reef Explorer Negril (its own guide page), Dressel Divers (Montego Bay and Lucea weekly plan) and Jamaica Scuba Divers (Runaway Bay). Resort Divers (Ocho Rios and Runaway Bay), One Love Scuba (Negril), Sandals and Beaches, and Garfield's Diving Station publish no site names, and Sun Divers, Negril Fun Diving and Marine Life Divers had no readable list. A site is counted when named on at least two independent lists (each operator once, the Tourist Board once). Almost every other site is on ScubaCaribe's maps alone, so it stays as an excluded one-list row rather than being dropped. Marley's Garden is on two lists but under two different towns, so it is held out until one shop confirms it. Magazines, blogs, PADI, Divessi and travel guides were used only for leads. No list gave coordinates. Counted 2026-10-14.",
